# A session cookie "<uid>.<version>.<expiry>:<tag>" holds while its tag, its expiry and its version hold
law session_cookie_valid
kind predicate
claim the cookie is "<uid>.<version>.<expiry>:<tag>" with decimal integers and a hex tag
claim the tag is the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA256 under the key, over the purpose "session", one zero byte and the text before the colon
claim the cookie holds strictly before its expiry, and only while its version is the current session version of the user
source a signed session cookie (the rule is stated here; nothing outside this file defines it)

use alice-sign hmac_sha256
const purpose text = "session"
const tag_bytes integer = 16

x-input cookie text
x-input now time
x-input key bytes
x-input user record(session_version: integer)

x-split cookie ":" head tag_hex
x-split head "." uid_text version_text expiry_text
x-bind uid uid_text integer
x-bind version version_text integer
x-bind expiry expiry_text time
x-bind tag tag_hex hex

require tag: tag == prefix(hmac_sha256(key, utf8(purpose) ++ 0x00 ++ utf8(head)), tag_bytes)
require fresh: now < expiry
require current: version == user.session_version

example {"cookie": "42.7.1893456000:b13155066f4d53246b4b26c896d79b7f", "now": 1893455000, "key": "000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f", "user": {"session_version": 7}}

verdict whether the cookie holds, and the first condition that does not
